A single-panel gag cartoon in the style of Gary Larson's The Far Side, about this news story.
Headline: {title}
Story: {summary}

First decide the joke: the one absurd or ironic truth behind the headline that everyone thinks but nobody says. Show it as ONE visual gag that someone who has only read the headline gets in two seconds: take a phrase from the story literally, swap who is in charge, or show where this ends up if nobody stops it. Ordinary people, animals or objects in an everyday place work best, rather than likenesses of the people named. Leave out the rest of the story's details.

Rules: one scene, no panels, borders or split screens. Two or three characters at most, each with the right number of arms, hands and legs. At most one short line of text in the whole picture (one speech bubble or one sign, under eight words, spelled correctly); no labels, logos or captions.
Style: black and white ink, bold clean outlines, crosshatched shading, plain white background, high contrast. {shape} picture that fills the whole canvas edge to edge. Keep the bottom quarter simple, just floor, ground or sky with no faces or text, because the headline is printed over it.
